Method A — ScreenPointToRay
Ray ray = Camera.main.ScreenPointToRay(Input.mousePosition);
Converts pixel position → world ray
✔ Used for clicking objects
✔ Converts a screen position (2D) → into a Ray (3D line) coming out from the camera through that pixel.
📌 Screen space = 2D (x,y)
📌 World space = 3D (x,y,z)
So this method creates a ray from the camera toward where the user clicked or touched.
✅ 1️⃣ Click-to-select Objects (Most Common Use Case)
Placing Objects in the World (Minecraft / building games)
✅ 4️⃣ Detecting Surfaces for Interactions
 Used for:
✔ Opening doors
✔ Picking up items
✔ Interacting with NPCs
✔ Highlighting objects

| **Purpose**                   | **What ScreenPointToRay Does**                  | **Example Code**                                                                | **Real Game Use Cases**                               |
| ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| **Select Object on Click**    | Converts mouse click to a ray to detect objects | `Ray ray = cam.ScreenPointToRay(Input.mousePosition);`                          | Selecting units, clicking items, inspecting 3D models |
| **FPS Shooting / Aiming**     | Creates a ray from center of screen             | `Ray ray = cam.ScreenPointToRay(new Vector3(Screen.width/2, Screen.height/2));` | FPS guns, laser pointers, aim assist                  |
| **Placing Objects in World**  | Finds world position under mouse                | `if (Physics.Raycast(ray, out hit)) place.position = hit.point;`                | Building systems, construction games, AR placement    |
| **Click-to-Move Character**   | Gets ground point to move player                | `if (Physics.Raycast(ray, out hit)) player.Move(hit.point);`                    | MOBA, RPG, strategy click-movement                    |
| **Interact With Objects**     | Checks if object is in front of camera          | `if (Physics.Raycast(ray, out hit)) Interact(hit.collider);`                    | Open doors, pick items, talk to NPCs                  |
| **Dragging 3D Objects**       | Converts screen drag to world ray               | `Physics.Raycast(ray, out hit);`                                                | 3D puzzle games, inventory systems                    |
| **Mobile Touch Input**        | Converts touch → ray                            | `Ray ray = cam.ScreenPointToRay(touch.position);`                               | Mobile interactions, AR apps                          |
| **Detecting Surface Type**    | Checks what surface was hit                     | `Debug.Log(hit.collider.tag);`                                                  | Footstep sounds, terrain type detection               |
| **Measure Distance**          | Use ray to detect distance to object            | `float d = hit.distance;`                                                       | Sniper zoom, object scanning                          |
| **Highlight Object on Hover** | Detect object under cursor every frame          | `if (Physics.Raycast(ray, out hit))`                                            | Outline effects, hover tooltips                       |


