Ray ray = new Ray(transform.position, transform.forward);
| **Part**                     | **Meaning**       | **Explanation**                                                 |
| ---------------------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `transform.position`         | **Ray Origin**    | The ray starts from the object’s world position.                |
| `transform.forward`          | **Ray Direction** | The ray goes in the direction the object is facing (blue axis). |
| `new Ray(origin, direction)` | Creates a ray     | A Ray is just a point + a direction.                            |

                       -----------------------------------------------


| Use Case                     | Why It Uses This Ray                                | Example                    |
| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| **Enemy AI vision**          | Enemy looks forward → ray checks if player is ahead | Detect player in front     |
| **Gun barrel shooting**      | Spawn bullets from gun muzzle forward               | FPS shooting               |
| **Obstacle detection**       | Character checks block in front before moving       | Prevent walking into walls |
| **Interaction**              | Door or object activates only when player faces it  | “Press E to open” systems  |
| **Line-of-sight checks**     | See if something blocks path                        | Stealth games              |
| **Car sensors / vehicle AI** | Forward sensors detect road/path                    | Racing games               |

